From: opiz3-wlan-backport
Subject: [PATCH] unisocwifi: wait for the disconnect event before returning

cfg80211 disconnect sent WIFI_CMD_DISCONNECT and returned at once. On a
Wi-Fi restart wpa_supplicant disconnects the station and deletes the
interface right after. In a repeater stress test (AP and station on the
radio, TEST-PLAN 2026-10-08) the teardown of a connected station either
asserted the firmware (rf_marlin.c line 1016, pri20_offset == NO_OFFSET)
or froze the board with no kernel output; the AP alone never did.

Wait up to 1 s for the firmware's disconnect event (it sets sm_state to
DISCONNECTED through sprdwl_report_disconnection) when the station was
connected. The vendor's SYNC_DISCONNECT wait exists for kernels before
4.9.60 only and is not built here.
---
diff --git a/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c b/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
index a31b2c7..bc589dc 100644
--- a/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
+++ b/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
@@ -2455,6 +2455,24 @@ static int sprdwl_cfg80211_disconnect(struct wiphy *wiphy,
 		vif->sm_state = old_state;
 		goto out;
 	}
+	/* Wait (up to 1 s) for the firmware's disconnect event before
+	 * returning. wpa_supplicant disconnects and deletes the interface
+	 * right after: with an AP on the radio too (repeater), deleting a
+	 * station context the firmware was still disconnecting asserted it
+	 * (rf_marlin.c pri20_offset) or froze the board. The event comes from
+	 * the SDIO RX path, which takes no lock held here.
+	 */
+	if (old_state == SPRDWL_CONNECTED) {
+		int i;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < 50 &&
+		     READ_ONCE(vif->sm_state) == SPRDWL_DISCONNECTING; i++)
+			msleep(20);
+		if (READ_ONCE(vif->sm_state) == SPRDWL_DISCONNECTING)
+			wl_ndev_log(L_ERR, ndev,
+				    "%s: no disconnect event within 1 s\n",
+				    __func__);
+	}
 #ifdef SYNC_DISCONNECT
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(4, 9, 60)
 	if (!sprdwl_sync_disconnect_event(vif, msecs_to_jiffies(1000))) {
